# ─── CREDENTIALS. The single most important lines in this file. ───────────────
#
# .clasprc.json holds a Google OAuth refresh token for the account that ran
# `clasp login`. Committing it hands anyone who can read the repo the ability to
# push code into your Apps Script projects. Treat it exactly as you would a
# password.
#
# `clasp login` normally writes it to your home directory, which is safely outside
# this repo. `clasp login --creds` or `--no-localhost` can put a copy in the
# working directory instead, which is how it ends up committed by accident.
.clasprc.json
**/.clasprc.json
*.credentials.json
client_secret*.json
.env
.env.*

# ─── NOT ignored, and on purpose ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# .clasp.json IS committed. It contains only the scriptId, which is not a secret —
# it identifies the project, it does not grant access to it. Committing it is what
# pins each folder to one specific project, which is what makes tools/preflight.mjs
# able to catch the A8 duplicate-project trap. Do not add it here.

# ─── Ordinary noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Jekyll build output, if Pages ever builds locally
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
